Hi,

I don't have access to the book, but here what I think the issue:

 #I believe it depends on how you construct the interaction:

 library(tidyr)

 #Given precision matrix Q1 of id_1:
 Q1 <- matrix(c(1,100,1000,10000),2,2)
 id_1 <- 1:2

 #Given precision matrix Q2 of id_2:
 Q2 <- matrix(c(1:9),3,3)
 id_2 <- 1:3

 #id of interaction can be constructed in two ways:

 #--> first way:
 id_inter_1 <- crossing(id_1,id_2)

 #which means I need to use:
 Q1%x%Q2

 #as the Krnocker product

 #--> second way:
 id_inter_2 <- crossing(id_2,id_1)

 #which means I need to use:
 Q2%x%Q1

 #as the Krnocker product. Note that id_1 and id_2 are different.

 This depends on how you construct your data (or id of the data), and this can be done in different ways:

 #One possible construction:

 Type 2: time %x% iid_space
 Type 3: space %x% iid_time

 When using the group feature for Type2 and Type3: make sure you add the correct number of constraints by using constr = TRUE and (when using RW2 by adding extra constraints using extraconstr)

